Interoperability

- The AirVPN adapter (`crates/providers/src/airvpn`; its `site/` and `status.rs` parts use
  AirVPN's website and public status API instead) is a separate Rust implementation of the
  bootstrap exchange of AirVPN's official client Eddie (GPL-3.0-or-later,
  https://github.com/AirVPN/Eddie). It was written with reference to Eddie's source at commit
  67e213bfeae270f1f26c62f454f9dfadd5342df9, and its handling of that exchange and of the server
  manifest follows the behaviour of that source. It uses the RSA public key and the four IPv4
  bootstrap addresses of Eddie's `resources/providers/AirVPN.json`, the exchange's parameter,
  element and attribute names, and Eddie's defaults for the WireGuard MTU (1320), the keepalive
  (15 s), `users_max` (100) and the server-load figure. A comparison with that commit found no
  text of Eddie's source files in the adapter apart from those values and names. Because the
  adapter follows Eddie's source in these ways, it is licensed under Eddie's licence,
  GPL-3.0-or-later, and not under the licences of the rest of this repository.
- The Mullvad adapter (`crates/providers/src/mullvad`) uses Mullvad's public API. Its paths,
  request bodies and response shapes were written with reference to the `mullvad-api` crate of
  the official app (GPL-3.0-or-later, https://github.com/mullvad/mullvadvpn-app). A line
  comparison with that crate's `access.rs`, `device.rs`, `relay_list.rs`, `rest.rs` and `lib.rs`
  at commit e8fd32f6bb7969e095b3a8056d3c39424861cd86 found no code in common beyond field names
  that the API's JSON fixes.
